1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,815
The outside pressure came from the ambassador of a country that had become famous for its cheap tickets.

2
00:00:05,815 --> 00:00:14,109
A banner on the wall read FREEDOM OF THE COAST, and a nationwide sweep had closed the little station by the fence.

3
00:00:14,109 --> 00:00:30,853
“A comprehensive review,” she said, “will tell us whether the road can cope.” About half the family had been born inland, and the rest had migrated to the mainland, and not one of them had been asked.

4
00:00:30,853 --> 00:00:40,386
Meanwhile the tonnage through the port had begun to fluctuate, and the odds of a second war had widened the breadth of every insurance table.

5
00:00:40,386 --> 00:00:50,860
A missile on a banner, a cool breeze from the sea, and a towel on the fence of the resort: the place had the makeup of a dull postcard.

6
00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:55,684
“Things vanish here,” the head of the local company said.

7
00:00:55,684 --> 00:01:00,044
“Slowly, and then all at once.”

8
00:01:00,044 --> 00:01:08,818
The transportation plan was a leap in the dark: a collaboration between an area office and a great house on the coast.

9
00:01:08,818 --> 00:01:19,201
A little car, a large door, and the name of a general on the letterhead gave it authority, and the startle it produced in the village was real.

10
00:01:19,201 --> 00:01:28,060
“Nothing about us without us,” the occupant of the second house said, and the ambassador wrote it down.

11
00:01:28,060 --> 00:01:31,460
The tremble in her voice was not fear.

12
00:01:31,460 --> 00:01:35,520
“The war blurred the map once,” she said.

13
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:53,088
“Do not let a blast of patriotism do it again.” A slipper by the door, an insertion in the local paper, and a broad sweep of the inland road were the only evidence they had, and it was enough to postpone the vote.

14
00:01:53,088 --> 00:01:58,642
What became clear was that they had to broaden the road without widening the gap.

15
00:01:58,642 --> 00:02:13,706
“Something has to change,” the ambassador said, “and it will not be the family.” The odds of that had faded from likely to possible, and the company had already begun to look for a second site.

16
00:02:13,706 --> 00:02:23,225
A crisp breeze, a cool evening, and a small crowd at the door: the pressure had arrived, and it had a name.

17
00:02:23,225 --> 00:02:33,288
The slow road home, the homeland behind the fence, and the same small crowd at the door: it was enough.
